Images

Physical images live here:

public/images/

Image references are centralized here:

src/data/images.js

IMAGE RULE — IMPORTANT

ONE PHYSICAL IMAGE = ONE FILE NAME.

A photo can be reused in Hero, Property cards, Property detail, About, Contact, Gallery, etc. by referencing the same path.

Do NOT save the same photo as:

villa01.jpg
about01.jpg
contact01.jpg

if all three are the same photo.

3. Adding a new image

Put the new photo in:

public/images/

Give it one clear filename, for example:

modern-villa-02.jpg

Add the reference in:

src/data/images.js

Example:

modernVilla02: "/images/modern-villa-02.jpg",

Use that reference wherever required.

Do not put public website images inside src/.

4. Google Maps / client location

Edit:

src/data/site.js

Set:

mapUrl: "CLIENT_GOOGLE_MAPS_SHARE_URL",

How to get the URL:

Open Google Maps.

Search for the client's business/location.

Click Share.

Copy the link.

Paste it into mapUrl.

The existing directions links will use that URL.

No Google Maps API key is required for this V1 directions-link approach.

5. Phone and WhatsApp

Phone:

phone: "+91 98765 43210",

WhatsApp must use international digits without +, spaces, or hyphens:

whatsapp: "919876543210",

The website generates the WhatsApp enquiry URL automatically.

6. Email

Edit:

email: "hello@company.com",

The Contact page uses this value automatically.

7. Files the client should normally NOT touch

Unless a developer is intentionally changing design or functionality, do not edit:

src/app/index.jsx
src/main.jsx
src/index.scss
src/styles/
src/components/
src/sections/
vite.config.js
package.json
package-lock.json
index.html

Do not randomly change imports, routes, component structure, or package configuration.

8. Normal update workflow

For a normal client update:

1. Edit src/data/site.js OR src/data/properties.js
2. Add new images only to public/images/
3. Update src/data/images.js when a new image is added
4. npm run dev
5. Check all pages and buttons
6. npm run lint
7. npm run build
8. Deploy the fresh dist/

9. Commands and when to use them

First setup on a new machine

npm install

Run once after receiving the project, or after dependency changes.

Local development

npm run dev

Open the URL printed by Vite.

This project is configured for local HTTPS. Typical URL:

https://localhost:5173/

A local certificate warning can be normal because the local certificate is not a public production certificate.

Lint

npm run lint

Use this to catch code-quality issues before delivery.

Production build

npm run build

Run after content, image, route, design, code, or dependency changes and always before deployment.

A successful build must finish without an error.

Preview production build locally

npm run preview

Use this to inspect the generated dist/ before publishing it.

10. HTTPS clarification

Local

The Vite development server can run over HTTPS:

npm run dev

Then use the HTTPS URL printed by Vite.

Production

Production HTTPS is provided by the hosting/domain/CDN layer.

The real production site should be accessed through something like:

https://www.clientdomain.com

Do not use the Vite development server or its local certificate as the production server/certificate.

11. Production deployment

The intended flow is:

Source project
    ↓
npm install
    ↓
npm run lint
    ↓
npm run build
    ↓
dist/
    ↓
Static hosting / CDN
    ↓
HTTPS domain

Deploy the generated dist/ directory.

Do not expose the Vite development server as production.

12. New-machine/client installation

The client/developer machine needs Node.js and npm.

Then:

cd path/to/real-estate-01
npm install
npm run dev

For final deployment:

npm run build

Then deploy:

dist/

