14. Troubleshooting

White page

Open:

F12 → Console

Look at the first red error.

Also run:

npm run build

Image not showing

Check the file exists in:

public/images/

Then check the exact path in:

src/data/images.js

Example:

"/images/villa01.jpg"

Filename and extension must match exactly.

Property detail not opening

Check src/data/properties.js and confirm:

The property has a unique id.

The property object exists.

Its image reference exists.

Phone not working

Check site.phone in src/data/site.js.

WhatsApp not working

Check site.whatsapp and remove +, spaces, and hyphens.

Directions not working

Check site.mapUrl and paste the client's current Google Maps Share URL.

15. Duplicate-image check

From the project root:

find public/images -type f -print0 | xargs -0 sha256sum | sort

If two different filenames have the same hash, they are likely duplicate copies of the same file.

The intended approach is:

ONE PHOTO
   ↓
ONE PHYSICAL FILE
   ↓
ONE CENTRAL IMAGE REFERENCE
   ↓
MANY SECTIONS CAN REUSE IT

